    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Copperas used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 543"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Sulphate of iron is used by hatters and dyers, when precipitated by gallic acid, for forming a black dye; it is also used for making ink; in the manufacture of Prussian blue; in preparing leather; and in forming colcothar for painters."@en ;
